<title>USA: Goldman Sachs's GS Financial Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Goldman Sachs's GS Financial Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>GS Financial Products U.S. LP, an indirect subsidiary of Goldman Sachs Group LP, said on Monday that its net income for the three months ended February 28, 1997 increased to $4.5 million from $3.1 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Revenues, net of interest expense, for the three-months increased to $4.8 million from $3.5 million a year ago, GS Financial said.</p>
<p>GS Financial is a derivative products company.</p>
</text>
